{
  "spec": 1,
  "what": "The written table the proposal robot answers to. Each case is an issue body as GitHub renders it, and what the robot must reply. It exists for the same reason cases.json does: the thing a stranger meets must be held to something written down, not to whatever the code happens to do today.",
  "read_by": [
    "tools/check-proposals.py, on every push to this repository"
  ],
  "always": [
    "the reply never contains a word from tools/words.json, whatever was sent in",
    "every fence the reply opens, it closes, so nothing a stranger wrote can escape into Markdown",
    "a case may carry `body_repeat` instead of `body`: one character, repeated. A table that spells out a 64 kB body is unreadable, and nobody would notice a mistake buried in it."
  ],
  "cases": [
